# `MEMBERSHIP-KEY-ACCEPTANCE`: the KEEP half. `in=` is withdrawn from TWO genres and
# from nothing else — a per-genre withdrawal is one genre's declaration
# lapsing, never the key leaving the language (core §3, `GENRE-VOCABULARY-OBLIGATION`), and the only way
# to say that in a fixture is to write the key where it is still legal.
#
# Two sections, because the two surviving genres are two independent
# declarations and a fixture that pinned only one would leave the other free
# to drift. Both still resolve `in=` against a declared `group` id, unchanged.
figdown 0.2 block
title "in= under block is untouched"
group g "Chassis"
node a "A" in=g

figdown 0.2 topology
title "in= under topology is untouched"
group site "Site 1"
node r1 "R1" in=site
